reopenReason:
DoD 2 asks the tests to show that 'recovery' passes ONLY WHEN cleanup deletes exactly the child's VM and leaves the foreign record intact. The tests do not show it. I ran mutation probes on the landed bytes (snapshot of 2cd85cc0, `node --test --test-name-pattern='^(LC|CF|CC)' scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs`). Each of the five conjuncts in `recovered()` (certify-lifecycle.mjs:88-90) can be deleted alone with every test still green:
- `theirs.phase !== 'deleted'`: the foreign-record guard;
- `report.deleted.length === 1`;
- `report.deleted[0] === record.instance`;
- `report.errors.length === 0`;
- `mine.phase === 'deleted'`.
LC3 only checks that the REAL cleanupOwned leaves the foreign record alone. No row makes the check face a cleanup that deletes the foreign record, or deletes more than the child's VM. So if cleanup broke, which is exactly what this probe certifies, nothing proves the probe would catch it.

Everything else holds:
- The verification command re-run on a snapshot of the commit: exit 0, 346 tests, 345 pass, 1 skipped (the opt-in macOS smoke).
- git diff --check is clean.
- Size: 396 changed / 330 net.
- The other 13 mutations were all killed: not-started, passed, timed-out, vm-deleted, record-live, the finally deleteOwned, the finally reap, the attempt-all-closed lookup, owned-only polling, errored, shell:true, no-reconcile and the reap timeout.
- DoD 1, DoD 3 and DoD 4 are met.

